# ── Firebase App Check ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# reCAPTCHA v3 site key (public key — safe to expose in client bundles).
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Go to https://www.google.com/recaptcha/admin
#      → Create site → reCAPTCHA v3 → add your domain(s)
#      → Copy the SITE KEY (not the secret key)
#
#   2. Go to Firebase Console → Build → App Check
#      → Register your web app → choose reCAPTCHA v3 → paste site key → Save
#
#   3. (Optional, recommended) Add a debug token for local dev:
#      → Run the app locally (npm run dev)
#      → Open browser console → look for "App Check debug token: <UUID>"
#      → Firebase Console → App Check → Apps → <your app> → Debug tokens → Add
#
#   4. When ready to enforce (blocks all unregistered clients):
#      → Firebase Console → App Check → each service → Enforce
#
#   5. Add VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY as a GitHub Actions secret so CI builds
#      also include App Check.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your value:
VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=your_recaptcha_v3_site_key_here
